====================================================================================================
  global rms |g| (arb units) = 3.49693
           delta bin      cells   <|g|^2>^1/2  ratio to global
        -1.0 to -0.5    1141965       3.49702           1.0000
        -0.5 to +0.0    1797662       3.49586           0.9997
        +0.0 to +0.5    1797159       3.49669           0.9999
        +0.5 to +1.0    1142094       3.49736           1.0001
        +1.0 to +3.0     599243       3.49855           1.0005
       +3.0 to +10.0        138       3.48967           0.9979
  PARITY PREDICTION: for a Gaussian field <g_i delta> = 0, so the ratio should be ~1 in
  every bin, i.e. acceleration statistically INDEPENDENT of local density.
  [OK] every delta bin has |g| within 0.21% of the global rms (range 0.9979-1.0005, threshold 0.85-1.20) -- the parity argument is CONFIRMED numerically: no density dependence at Gaussian order

